  "note": "Triennial election of the electoral divisions of Irvinestown rural district, one member each, polled on 2 June 1949. Garrison was the only contested division; the Fermanagh Herald prints the other nominations, showing one change of member. The traditionally Nationalist seat was retained by Casey. The result is printed as 139 to 131 in the Fermanagh Herald; the News-Letter gave 138 to 131."
